From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: f0xeri <9pik.official@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:43:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] qwz: keep msi_ce_irqmask up to date in one-MSI mode

qwz_pcic_ce_irq_enable()/_disable() return early in one-MSI mode before
updating sc->msi_ce_irqmask, but qwz_ce_intr() ignores copy engines
whose bit is not set in it in both modes. With a single MSI vector (all
macOS gives us: IOPCIFamily has no multi-message MSI and the chip has no
MSI-X) every copy engine interrupt is then treated as unexpected: the
HTC control response arrives only through the polling fallback and the
HTT service connect times out, so the device never comes up. Update the
mask before the one-MSI early return.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/dev/pci/if_qwz_pci.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/dev/pci/if_qwz_pci.c b/sys/dev/pci/if_qwz_pci.c
index 8ce128ef3cac18173de887ac3e43f190ba438edf..432bbdd3d2afda81f717973c48c917a736dad285 100644
--- a/sys/dev/pci/if_qwz_pci.c
+++ b/sys/dev/pci/if_qwz_pci.c
@@ -1439,6 +1439,9 @@ qwz_pcic_ext_irq_enable(struct qwz_softc *sc)
 void
 qwz_pcic_ce_irq_enable(struct qwz_softc *sc, uint16_t ce_id)
 {
+#ifdef QWZMAC /* QWZMAC: qwz_ce_intr() checks the mask in one-MSI mode too */
+	sc->msi_ce_irqmask |= (1U << ce_id);
+#endif
 	/* In case of one MSI vector, we handle irq enable/disable in a
 	 * uniform way since we only have one irq
 	 */
@@ -1452,6 +1455,9 @@ qwz_pcic_ce_irq_enable(struct qwz_softc *sc, uint16_t ce_id)
 void
 qwz_pcic_ce_irq_disable(struct qwz_softc *sc, uint16_t ce_id)
 {
+#ifdef QWZMAC /* QWZMAC: qwz_ce_intr() checks the mask in one-MSI mode too */
+	sc->msi_ce_irqmask &= ~(1U << ce_id);
+#endif
 	/* In case of one MSI vector, we handle irq enable/disable in a
 	 * uniform way since we only have one irq
 	 */
